---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Community & Courses | Liberating Scripture Collective"
  description="Courses, study companions, and community spaces for reading scripture with context, care, and critical honesty. Built together, not delivered from above."
  canonical="https://liberatingscripture.org/community/"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script
      type="application/ld+json"
      is:inline
      set:html={JSON.stringify({
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "@type": "WebPage",
        "@id": "https://liberatingscripture.org/community/#webpage",
        url: "https://liberatingscripture.org/community/",
        name: "Community & Courses | Liberating Scripture Collective",
        isPartOf: { "@id": "https://liberatingscripture.org/#website" },
      })}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="community-page">
    <header class="community-hero">
      <div class="content">
        <p class="eyebrow">Collective</p>
        <h1>Community &amp; Courses</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          This is where the "Collective" part is most literal. Not a service you
          subscribe to, but a space we build together.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="community-content content">
      <section class="community-section" aria-labelledby="community-what">
        <h2 id="community-what">What this is</h2>
        <p>
          Most religious education runs in one direction: expert to student,
          institution to individual, producer to consumer. The Liberating
          Scripture Collective is trying to build something different.
        </p>
        <p>
          This space is for courses, study companions, and collaborative
          learning environments where people contribute, not just receive. Think
          of it as
          <strong>spiritual mutual aid</strong>: people with different
          backgrounds and experiences coming together around scripture,
          theology, liberation, and healing, each bringing what they know, each
          learning from others.
        </p>
        <p>
          Accessibility is built in, not bolted on. No seminary degree required.
          No gatekeeping. No paywalls for core content.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="community-section" aria-labelledby="community-developing">
        <h2 id="community-developing">What's taking shape</h2>

        <div class="community-grid">
          <article class="community-card">
            <h3>Study companions</h3>
            <p>
              Reading guides for the LIT Bible that provide context, questions,
              and connections, designed for individuals, small groups, and
              communities.
            </p>
            <span class="status-label">In development</span>
          </article>

          <article class="community-card">
            <h3>Short courses</h3>
            <p>
              Focused, accessible courses on translation, biblical history,
              liberation theology, and trauma-informed faith. Built to be
              digestible, honest, and practically useful.
            </p>
            <span class="status-label">In development</span>
          </article>

          <article class="community-card">
            <h3>Collaborative spaces</h3>
            <p>
              Places for readers, scholars, practitioners, artists, and people
              with lived experience to think together, contribute insights,
              raise questions, and shape the work.
            </p>
            <span class="status-label">Coming soon</span>
          </article>

          <article class="community-card">
            <h3>Peer learning</h3>
            <p>
              Structured conversations and cohorts where people learn from one
              another, not just from content. Because interpretation happens in
              community.
            </p>
            <span class="status-label">Coming soon</span>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section
        class="community-section community-section--contribute"
        aria-labelledby="community-contribute"
      >
        <h2 id="community-contribute">Help build it</h2>
        <p>
          This space is genuinely unfinished, and that's intentional. The people
          who show up get to help shape what it becomes.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you have something to contribute: experience with adult education,
          community organizing, biblical scholarship, accessibility, curriculum
          development, or just clarity about what you've needed and couldn't
          find, reach out. This is an invitation to collaborate, not a waiting
          list.
        </p>
        <div class="community-actions">
          <a href="/contact/" class="btn"><span>Get in touch</span></a>
          <a href="/support/" class="btn btn--outline"
            ><span>Support the work</span></a
          >
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .community-hero {
    background: var(--ink);
    color: #c8c6c0;
    padding: clamp(3.5rem, 7vw, 6rem) 0;
  }

  .community-hero .content {
    max-width: 64ch;
  }

  .community-hero h1 {
    font-family: "Crimson Text", Georgia, serif;
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4.5vw, 3.8rem);
    color: var(--cream);
    margin: 0.75rem 0 1.25rem;
  }

  .community-hero .eyebrow {
    color: #3abf6a;
  }
  .community-hero .lede {
    color: #c8c6c0;
    max-width: 52ch;
  }

  .community-content {
    padding: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem) 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 3.5rem;
  }

  .community-content .community-section:first-child {
    max-width: 64ch;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .community-section h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 2.5vw, 2rem);
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
  }

  .community-section p {
    max-width: 68ch;
  }

  .community-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .community-card {
    background: var(--surface-raised);
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 1.75rem;
    box-shadow: 0 2px 16px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .community-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .community-card p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--text);
    margin: 0;
    max-width: none;
    flex: 1;
  }

  .status-label {
    font-family: Inter, sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--green);
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .community-section--contribute {
    background: var(--surface-raised);
    border-radius: 20px;
    padding: 2.5rem;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 24px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.07);
  }

  .community-section--contribute h2 {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .community-actions {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .community-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
